WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.801
-Welcome back. Did you --

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.367
That was stressful.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.567
I have, like, quite
an adrenaline rush right now.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:07.801
-You do?
-Yes, I do.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:08.934
-But do you like this?

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:09.868
Is this the way
we should always do it?

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.033
A game with you before we talk?

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.267
-Yeah, it kind of breaks the ice
in a nice way.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.601
My heart rate is
still really high.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.067
-I'm very competitive.
I'm sorry about that, yeah.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.400
-I didn't know that I would be
decent, actually.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.567
And I -- So that was --
that's good.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:24.767
-You were phenomenal,
by the way.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.267
-I felt like I was okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.801
-You were more than decent.
You were more than decent.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.767
-I just thought it was going to
be real bad,

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.901
and I wasn't as bad as, well.
-This interesting though to me

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.300
because last time you were
on the show,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.601
we were talking about
"Doctor Strange."

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.167
-Yes, we were.
-And you were like, "I don't --

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:39.567
I don't -- Jimmy, I don't know.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.901
I never know if the movie is
going to be big or not big.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.701
I just don't know. I do my best
and blah, blah, blah."

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.467
And I go,
"It's going to be giant."

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.300
You were like, "I just don't --
I don't know."

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.767
And it went on to make
over $950 million.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.100
-I don't know.
-Almost a billion dollars.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I don't know.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:54.868
-What do you mean
you don't know?

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:55.901
-No, but I guess it did. It did.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.501
-It definitely did it.
Yes, it did.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.734
It's a giant, massive hit.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.334
-That's a wild number.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.601
-It's an insane number.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:04.634
-It's a weird number that I
can't really --

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.234
I don't know what
to equate it to, those numbers.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.901
-But you haven't seen it still?

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.400
-No, I haven't seen it still.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.767
-Yeah. Is it because, just,
you don't see your own movies?

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.133
Are you one of those?
-I wish.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.834
No, I'm not one of those.
I'm like one of those people

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.567
who, like, wants to study
something so I can figure out

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.234
how to make it better.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.767
So you just haven't gotten
around to it.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.868
-No. I had a cold when we had
the premiere,

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.033
and I didn't want to
sit through it.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.601
-You did have a cold?
-I did have a cold.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.467
-I remember that.
-And then I -- Yes,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:30.000
because I was here,
and you gave me that spray.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.667
-Yeah. Did it work?
-It was fabulous.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.133
-Alright, good.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:37.734
And so I asked them to send me
a copy so I could watch it.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.767
And it was -- like, it had
my name on it,

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.334
and then it had
the time I was watching it

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.634
And I didn't want to watch it
like that.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.968
-Oh, because it's Marvel,
it's very tricky when you --

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.367
-Yes.
-They call them the screeners.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.100
And if they give you a screener
of a movie,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.133
you go, "Oh, my gosh."
But they put a watermark on it

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:53.000
in case you somehow sell it
illegally.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.934
-Yeah, so my name would be on
it, and the exact time and date.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.534
-Imagine if you did that.
-And it was just distracting.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:00.901
Could you imagine
if I did do that?

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.033
-It doesn't seem like you
at all, to me, to do that.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.000
-How do you even do that?
Like, who do you send it to?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.634
Like, how do you even record it
on a computer?

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.033
-I tried to do it
when I was a kid

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.501
in high school with two VCRs.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.501
-That's how I watched
the Olympics.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.868
I would leave a VHS tape
in the TV

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.701
and then I would record it
while I was at school.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:19.300
-Well, I think you're allowed to
do that.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.601
-Oh, yeah, yeah,
you're allowed to.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:21.534
You're trying to do something
illegal.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.667
-I was doing something illegal.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.133
Yeah, and I got busted.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.033
They had a thing. It would go
dark and light, dark and light

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.634
and it was clearly -- I couldn't
make money that way, yeah.

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:31.467
-Whoa, you were trying to
bootleg stuff

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.801
like on the streets
of your school?

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.467
-No, no, no, I think just make
a copy for myself.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.934
I didn't have to keep renting
"Pee-Wee's Big Adventure."

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.067
[ Laughter ]
-I see. I see.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.501
-"I can't keep doing this."

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.367
Are you going to do more Marvel?

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.367
-I hope so.

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:48.701
They don't tell me anything
about my fate. So I --

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.767
-They don't even let you know
that you're coming back?

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.467
-No. I don't know.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.367
-But you're --
I mean, you can --

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.801
-I should come back.
-Yeah, of course.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Of course you should come back.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.267
-But I really -- I don't know.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.767
I want, like, fans to be,
like, so aggressive, you know,

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.100
and, like, terrify them into
doing it or something.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.934
I mean, that's not a good way
to do anything actually.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.434
I really take that back.
-Well, the fans love you.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:13.434
-Yeah. No one needs to use,
like, force.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.133
-No. We love you.
We just want to see more of you.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.300
-I would love to do more.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.234
-"WandaVision," you just crushed
that as well.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:20.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.033
I would do that --

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.934
I would love any -- I would love
any of the -- all of the above.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.934
All of the above.
-Yeah. And I'll watch the movie.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.434
-Yes.
-It's streaming, I heard.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.534
-Yes, it is. There you go.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:33.067
And your name will be on it just
for a little bit at the top.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:35.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:37.334
-And then you're in
the whole movie.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.634
Can we talk about this?
-Yes, please.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:42.100
-Last time you were here,
we unveiled the cover

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.467
"Hattie Harmony:
Worry Detective."

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.367
And I was very excited
because I love kids books.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:47.734
-Yes.
You write beautiful kids books.

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:50.000
-No, no, but I just love reading
them too.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.067
Trust me. There couldn't be more
kids books written in the world

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.734
'cause I just need -- I'm tired
of the same book.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.701
I've read them. I've tried to
push them to the other side

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.634
of the room, they keep ending
back and I'm like,

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:03.400
"Alright, let's read it again.
'Good Night, Moon,' here we go!"

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.167
And it's good, but I'm ready for
some new classics.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.901
But this one,
tell me about this.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.667
You wrote this during
the pandemic with your...?

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.267
-Yes, I did, with my husband.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.234
And we were already wanting to

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.200
write children's books
pre-pandemic.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.234
And it made sense to write one
about children's mental wellness

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:25.200
or really just dealing with
worries and anxieties for kids

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.400
and teaching them emotional
language for the first time.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.801
So, it's "Hattie Harmony: Worry
Detective," and she is a cat

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.868
who goes to school called
Wildwood Elementary.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:38.601
And she helps her friends
identify their worries.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:41.067
And then she gives them tools
on how to deal with it.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:43.901
-It's so cute. I love it.
[ Applause ]

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:46.834
Marissa Valdez does
the illustrations.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.067
-Yeah, very cute illustrations.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.400
If I do say so myself.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.467
-Yeah, I love the --

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.000
This is where someone has
butterflies in their stomach,

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.834
and she gets a butterfly net
to get them out.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.801
-Pearl Peppercorn,
the porcupine,

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.667
has butterflies in her stomach.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.801
-I saw there's -- there's this
photo that you and your husband

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.667
have been doing that's going
around on the Internet.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.801
-Yeah.
-Of I want to say flat Hattie?

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.501
-Flat Hatties.
-Flat Hatties.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.534
-Yeah.
-Yeah. This is flat Hattie.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:13.734
Where are you here?

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:16.367
-We're in Italy pre-getting
COVID.

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.767
-Yeah. This is before, yeah.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:22.868
-Yeah, and so, we'd take Hattie
with us wherever we'd go.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:27.267
And my husband carries her
literally everywhere --

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.434
the gym, Dodger games.
-Yeah.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:33.801
I love that -- here it is --
-We're really big Dodger fans.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.267
-You're giant Dodger fans.
-We're giant Dodger fans.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:39.501
And so, every single player with
a kid on the team,

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.100
they don't know this yet,

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.701
but they will be getting
a "Hattie Harmony."

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.767
[ Laughter and applause ]
-'Cause you love them that much?

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.334
-We love the Dodgers.
-But anyone out there, you can

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:51.300
draw your Hattie Harmonys
and start Flat Hattie'ing

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.467
around wherever you are.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:56.000
Is it true that I heard
Hattie is here tonight?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.234
-It is true.
-Somewhere in the audience.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.200
-She's a really big fan.
-She's a fan?

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.234
-She's a big fan of "The Tonight
Show" and the Roots.

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:05.000
-And the Roots, of course.
-And so she wanted to be here.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.400
-Can we see her?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.367
Oh, there she is. Oh, my gosh.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.534
-And that's my beautiful
husband, Robbie Arnett.

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:16.300
-And, of course, that is
your awesome husband.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.667
Hey, buddy, good to see you,
pal.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:19.167
Congrats on the book.

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:21.300
Congratulations on the book.
Have a great summer.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.767
Thank you for being here.
Thanks for playing.

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.534
Elizabeth Olsen, everybody.

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:27.601
"Hattie Harmony: Worry
Detective" is available now.

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:30.467
Gaten Matarazzo joins us
after the break. Stick around.

